in our ongoing series school matters  we're looking at the debates over  how and when to reopen schools safely  but some things are not a matter of  debate they are settled fact and that is  this it's a challenging time for  teachers that goes  for teachers returning to the classroom  but also those teachers who are  continuing to work  online so what we're going to do this  morning is we want to say thank you to  just a few of the teachers  who've had such a big impact on people's  lives students all over the country what  we did is we asked four successful  americans  i think you've heard of them bill gates  chelsea clinton musician josh groban  and actor levar burton we wanted them to  tell us about the teachers  who've inspired them hi i'm bill gates  i'm josh groban i am chelsea clinton i'm  levar burton  fawn is here here back to school  one of my most influential teachers has  got to be mrs twigg  third grade hannah american elementary  in hanow germany  on certain rainy afternoons mrs twigg  would put me in front of the class  and have me read while she went to the  teacher's lounge to make herself  a cup of tea i was the best reader in  my third grade class and it was the  first time  in my life that somebody outside of my  family recognized that  i was good at cycling i had a talent  gift  it's one of my favorite fables the  tortoise and the hair  great teachers help students get excited  about  learning mrs blanche caffierre  a teacher at view ridge elementary  school in seattle was that kind of  teacher for me  i was a very shy 4th grader with a messy  desk and terrible handwriting  i tried to hide the fact that i loved to  read because i was worried it would look  strange to my classmates mrs cappier  pulled me out of my shell by sharing her  love of books  she pushed me to read challenging ones  and then asked me interesting questions  that made me think  about what i'd read she listened to what  i had to say  looking back on it now there's no  question that she helped spark my love  for learning and helped inspire  the gates foundation's work to help  every child in america  get the benefit of great teachers  i want to give a huge thanks to the late  great norman cohen my theater teacher at  the los angeles county high school for  the arts for giving me my first lead  role in a play  and my musical theater teacher there  gary sorensen who gave me my first  lead role in a musical if i were a rich  man  [Music]  having the arts in my life as a student  just changed my life  as a shy introverted kid who had a  really hard time expressing myself  having the arts as a tool to do that not  only opened up a world of possibility  for me but i know it does it for  millions of kids  around the world  i'm so profoundly grateful to dr sadie  mitchell who was my first grade teacher  at forest park elementary school in  little rock arkansas  dr mitchell set the bar for what an  extraordinary  teacher should be and she did it every  day  she did it in helping us work on our  penmanship  she did it in helping us learn to count  and she did it whenever we had a bad day  by reminding us that tomorrow was a new  day  i just hope that i'm able to have even a  little bit of the same effect on some of  my students today  and i hope that every student is as  lucky as i was to have a dr mitchell  in their lives thank you to the great  teachers and the arts teachers out there  who are bringing a spark of humanity  into our classrooms  when we need it in this world more than  ever i can't tell you how important it  is to have somebody  recognize our potential to see it and  nurture it thank you this is  so as teachers get ready to welcome  students back to their classroom  either in person or virtually i want to  say thank you for your dedication  you're changing lives and doing amazing  work  and guys i know we're going to have a  lot to say about that segment but before  we do i just want to have a little  reminder here uh for people out there  watching if you have a teacher who came  to mind as you were watching that a  teacher who inspired you  we want to hear from you find us on  social media share your story and we  might  even feature it on a future segment  because teacher appreciation does not  end with this segment right here it goes  on and on galen anthony yeah it sure  does  and one great teacher literally can  change your life  you really can you see that right there
 

